artifactory:index/oauthSettings:OauthSet.description:
This resource can be used to manage Artifactory's OAuth SSO settings.

Only a single <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`artifactory.OauthSettings`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`artifactory.OauthSettings`" pulumi-lang-go="`OauthSettings`" pulumi-lang-python="`OauthSettings`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`artifactory.OauthSettings`" pulumi-lang-java="`artifactory.OauthSettings`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`artifactory_oauth_settings`">`artifactory.OauthSettings`</span> resource is meant to be defined.

~>The <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`artifactory.OauthSettings`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`artifactory.OauthSettings`" pulumi-lang-go="`OauthSettings`" pulumi-lang-python="`OauthSettings`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`artifactory.OauthSettings`" pulumi-lang-java="`artifactory.OauthSettings`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`artifactory_oauth_settings`">`artifactory.OauthSettings`</span> resource utilizes endpoints which are blocked/removed in SaaS environments (i.e. in Artifactory online), rendering this resource incompatible with Artifactory SaaS environments.

## Example Usage

